B.aVg=s(["1. Give the picture before you give the thing. The child picks up a picture, you take it, and the thing arrives immediately. That order is the whole method.","2. Two adults makes phase 1 easier. One sits behind the child and helps their hand to the picture; the other holds the thing and waits. Say nothing during the exchange \u2014 no \u201csay water\u201d, no prompts.","3. Photograph what your child actually owns. Their cup, their blanket, their teacher. A stock picture is fine; their own cup is better.","4. Keep it to one word. \u201cBrushing\u201d, not \u201ctime to brush your teeth\u201d. The picture carries the meaning; the word is a label.","5. Never take the picture away as a punishment, and never make the child \u201cask nicely\u201d before you respond in the early phases. The exchange must always work.","6. Move up a phase when it works most of the time for two or three days. If it stops working, drop back one phase \u2014 that is normal, not failure.","7. Do not remove speech. If the child starts to say the word, say it back and still honour the picture. The picture is the floor, not the ceiling."],t.s)
