B.bqE=new A.qf(1,"Give the picture.","Give one picture",'Put ONE picture in front of the child and nothing else. When they pick it up, take it, hand over the thing immediately, and say the single word once. No questions, no "say it". The picture is the request \u2014 that is the whole lesson.',0,"exchange")
B.bqC=new A.qf(2,"Bring it to me.","Distance and persistence","Move the picture a step away, then across the room, then into a book. The child should get the picture, bring it to you, and put it in your open hand. Wait them out: one step further every two or three days.",1,"distance")
B.wP=new A.qf(3,"Which one?","Choose between pictures","Offer two pictures for two different things, and only give what they actually handed you. If they give the wrong one, hand back what they chose \u2014 calmly \u2014 and let them swap. Add a third picture when the pair is reliable.",2,"discrimination")
B.bqB=new A.qf(4,"I want\u2026","Build a sentence",'The board now has a strip. They put the "want" picture, then the thing they want, then speak or hand you the strip. Read the strip back as you hand the item over.',3,"sentence")
B.bqD=new A.qf(5,"What do you want?","Answer a question",'Now the adult speaks first: "What do you want?" and the child builds the strip in reply. Keep it to one question at a time, and never ask twice in a row.',4,"respond")
B.bqA=new A.qf(6,"I see\u2026","Comment, not just ask","Requests only get things. Comments get attention. Add the comment starters \u2014 I see, I hear, it is \u2014 and answer every comment as if it were the most interesting thing you have heard today, because to them it is.",5,"comment")
